# 🤓: This is a pattern__learn datum (PRD-007 sub-stereotype of learn).
# Agents bless the /next-task: pattern after reading all sections.

## OODA Handoff Schema

# When an agent completes a task it MUST emit a handoff in this format:
#
# ```toml
# [handoff]
# completed_task = 24          # b00t task ID just finished
# tier = "sm0l"                # who did it
# artifacts = [                # what was produced (verifiable)
#   "b00t-cli/src/datum_utils.rs:type_tags filter",
#   "cargo test: 550 pass",
# ]
# otel_summary = "cmds=12 guard_hits=3 postel=2"  # from b00t session otel
# blockers = []                # task IDs or descriptions blocking further progress
# next_task = 25               # pre-selected lowest unblocked by priority
# next_tier = "ch0nky"         # routing decision
# next_cmd = "b00t task next"  # literal command to continue
# stop_conditions = [          # when to stop this loop
#   "all P1 tasks complete",
#   "B00T_OTEL_ENDPOINT health check fails",
# ]
# ```

## /next-task:N Protocol

# The pattern `/next-task:N` in b00t means:
# 1. Current task (implicitly the one the agent was working on) is DONE
# 2. N = next task ID pre-selected by the agent
# 3. Hand off context compressed to: handoff TOML + OTEL summary + 3 artifact refs
# 4. Next agent boots with: `b00t task get N` + handoff context only
#
# This is the "digital thread" in practice: each handoff IS an entry in the thread.
# The thread is queryable: `b00t task list --handoff-chain` (future CLI).

## Resource Gate

# Before each /next-task:N, the orchestrator MUST check:
# ```
# b00t hive status   # GPU/RAM gate for ch0nky/frontier tier
# b00t task next     # confirms N is still highest priority unblocked
# ```
# If resource gate fails → handoff includes `blocked_by = "resource:gpu_mb=24000"`.

## OODA Loop Instance

# ```
# [OBSERVE]  b00t session otel --scrape → metrics
#            b00t datum filter --types=okr → KR status
# [ORIENT]   b00t task next → identify next P1 unblocked task
#            b00t whoami --role=<tier> → load role context (delta if available)
# [DECIDE]   guard eval → tier assignment (sm0l/ch0nky/frontier)
#            resource gate (b00t hive status)
# [ACT]      @tier: b00t task get N; implement/fix/verify
#            cargo test (sm0l) OR cargo build (ch0nky) → verify
#            b00t task done N → emit handoff → /next-task:M
# [LOOP]
# ```

## Acceptance Criteria (Pattern Blessing)

# - [ ] Agent emits handoff TOML after every task completion
# - [ ] Handoff includes OTEL summary from b00t session otel
# - [ ] next_task is the ACTUAL `b00t task next` output (not a guess)
# - [ ] Handoff fits in ≤200 tokens (compressed context)
# - [ ] Thread continuity: each handoff references completed_task ID

